==Production==
===Development===
In September 2016, after going through several incarnations and various stages of development for over a year, [[Mara Brock Akil]], her husband Salim Akil, and perennial [[Warner Bros. Television]] producer [[Greg Berlanti]] began pitching ''Black Lightning'' to television networks. The Akils wrote the script while serving as [[executive producer]]s alongside Berlanti and his frequent collaborator Sarah Schechter.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2016/09/black-lightning-dc-superhero-series-greg-berlanti-mara-brock-akil-salim-akil-1201811892/|title='Black Lightning' DC Superhero Series In Works From Greg Berlanti, Mara Brock Akil & Salim Akil|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Andreeva|first=Nellie|date=September 1, 2016|access-date=May 11, 2017|archive-date=May 20, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170520101618/http://deadline.com/2016/09/black-lightning-dc-superhero-series-greg-berlanti-mara-brock-akil-salim-akil-1201811892/|url-status=live}}</ref> A week later, the project landed at [[Fox Broadcasting Company|Fox]] with a pilot production commitment.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2016/09/black-lightning-fox-dc-superhero-drama-series-greg-berlanti-mara-brock-salim-akil-1201815368/|title=Fox Nabs 'Black Lightning' DC Superhero Drama With Pilot Production Commitment|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Andreeva|first=Nellie|date=September 8, 2016|access-date=May 11, 2017|archive-date=April 29, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170429131634/http://deadline.com/2016/09/black-lightning-fox-dc-superhero-drama-series-greg-berlanti-mara-brock-salim-akil-1201815368/|url-status=live}}</ref> In February 2017, Fox opted to not go forward with the pilot, deciding that it was "not a good fit into its already crowded genre drama space" and the project was subsequently shopped to other networks. As the home to several of Berlanti's other television ventures, [[The CW]] emerged as the network that was likely to realize the series.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2017/02/black-lightning-dc-comic-drama-move-the-cw-greg-berlanti-1201901139/|title='Black Lightning' Drama Eyes Move To the CW To Join Greg Berlanti Comic Lineup|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Andreeva|first=Nellie|date=February 2, 2017|access-date=May 11, 2017|archive-date=May 8, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170508211323/http://deadline.com/2017/02/black-lightning-dc-comic-drama-move-the-cw-greg-berlanti-1201901139/|url-status=live}}</ref> The following day, The CW officially ordered a pilot for ''Black Lightning''.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2017/02/black-lightning-dc-drama-the-cw-pilot-order-greg-berlanti-mara-brock-akil-salim-1201901901/|title='Black Lightning' DC Drama From Greg Berlanti & 'The Game' Duo Gets The CW Pilot Order|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Andreeva|first=Nellie|date=February 3, 2017|access-date=May 11, 2017|archive-date=May 8, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170508194943/http://deadline.com/2017/02/black-lightning-dc-drama-the-cw-pilot-order-greg-berlanti-mara-brock-akil-salim-1201901901/|url-status=live}}</ref> The original pilot script that had been written for Fox was discarded and instead, a short presentation was shot ahead of the network's final decisions regarding pickup orders.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2017/04/pilots-2017-early-buzz-primetime-broadcast-networks-1202063678/|title=PILOTS 2017: Very, Very Early Buzz Edition|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Andreeva|first=Nellie|date=April 12, 2017|access-date=May 11, 2017|archive-date=May 8, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170508211640/http://deadline.com/2017/04/pilots-2017-early-buzz-primetime-broadcast-networks-1202063678/|url-status=live}}</ref>

The CW officially ordered ''Black Lightning'' to series on May 10, 2017, with Salim Akil to serve as [[showrunner]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2017/05/black-lightning-life-sentence-series-the-cw-1202089253/|title='Black Lightning' & Lucy Hale's 'Life Sentence' Picked Up To Series By The CW|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Andreeva|first=Nellie|date=May 10, 2017|access-date=May 11, 2017|archive-date=May 11, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170511194156/http://deadline.com/2017/05/black-lightning-life-sentence-series-the-cw-1202089253/|url-status=live}}</ref> On April 2, 2018, The CW renewed the series for a second season, which premiered on October 9, 2018.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/riverdale-flash-supernatural-10-cw-renewals-1098997|title='Riverdale,' 'Flash,' 'Supernatural' Among 10 CW Renewals|website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|last=Goldberg|first=Lesley|date=April 2, 2018|access-date=April 2, 2018|archive-date=April 2, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180402195748/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/riverdale-flash-supernatural-10-cw-renewals-1098997|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Swift">{{Cite web|url=https://www.tvline.com/news/cw-premiere-dates-fall-2018-flash-charmed-riverdale-954928/|title=The CW Sets Fall Premiere Dates, Including New 'Super' Sunday|website=[[TVLine]]|last=Swift|first=Andy|date=June 20, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180620225706/https://tvline.com/2018/06/20/cw-premiere-dates-fall-2018-flash-charmed-riverdale/|archive-date=June 20, 2018|url-status=live|access-date=June 20, 2018}}</ref> On January 31, 2019, The CW renewed the series for a third season, which premiered on October 7, 2019.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/cw-renews-flash-charmed-riverdale-supernatural-6-more-1181714|title=CW Renews 'The Flash,' 'Charmed,' 'Riverdale,' 'Supernatural,' 6 More|website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|last=Goldberg|first=Lesley|date=January 31, 2019|access-date=January 31, 2019|archive-date=February 2, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190202015411/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/cw-renews-flash-charmed-riverdale-supernatural-6-more-1181714|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="S3">{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2019/08/black-lightning-premiere-date-season-3-moves-1202660796/|title='Black Lightning' Season 3 Premiere Bolts Two Weeks Earlier – TCA|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Hipes|first=Patrick|date=August 4, 2019|access-date=August 4, 2019|archive-date=August 4, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190804164816/https://deadline.com/2019/08/black-lightning-premiere-date-season-3-moves-1202660796/|url-status=live}}</ref> On January 7, 2020, the series was renewed for a fourth season, which premiered on February 8, 2021.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.tvline.com/news/the-cw-renewed-shows-2020-list-riverdale-flash-1142188/|title=CW Renews Riverdale, Batwoman, Roswell, Black Lightning Plus 9 Others|website=[[TVLine]]|last=Ausiello|first=Michael|date=January 7, 2020|access-date=January 7, 2020|archive-date=January 8, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200108032431/https://tvline.com/2020/01/07/the-cw-renewed-shows-2020-list-riverdale-flash/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="S4PremiereDate">{{cite web|url=https://www.tvline.com/news/the-cw-premiere-dates-2021-the-flash-superman-and-lois-1234589328/|title=The CW Sets Delayed Premiere Dates for Flash, Superman & Lois, Riverdale, Charmed, Batwoman and More|last=Ausiello|first=Michael|work=[[TVLine]]|date=October 29, 2020|access-date=October 29, 2020|archive-date=October 29, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201029222037/https://tvline.com/2020/10/29/the-cw-premiere-dates-2021-the-flash-superman-and-lois/|url-status=live}}</ref> On November 20, 2020, The CW confirmed that the fourth season will be the final season of the series.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2020/11/black-lightning-end-fourth-season-on-the-cw-1234619591/|title='Black Lightning' To End With Season 4 On the CW|website=Deadline Hollywood|first=Denise|last=Petski|date=November 20, 2020|access-date=November 20, 2020|archive-date=November 20, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201120181755/https://deadline.com/2020/11/black-lightning-end-fourth-season-on-the-cw-1234619591/|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Writing===
In order to have an "authentic black voice" for its setting and characters, ''Black Lightning'' utilizes a predominantly African-American writing staff.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://m.zimbio.com/TV+News/articles/XPTOqA3g5Ek/Black+Lightning+Will+Wokest+Superhero+TV|title=Here's Why Black Lightning Will Be the Wokest Superhero on TV|website=Zimbio|last=Abid|first=Areeba|date=July 22, 2017|access-date=June 1, 2019|archive-date=June 4, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190604051257/http://m.zimbio.com/TV%2BNews/articles/XPTOqA3g5Ek/Black%2BLightning%2BWill%2BWokest%2BSuperhero%2BTV|url-status=live}}</ref> Salim Akil shared that the writers are not all African-American but "have either lived this life or know someone who has."<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2018/01/black-lightning-salim-akil-dc-comic-black-voices-tv-turned-corner-tca-1202237371/|title='Black Lightning' Showrunner Salim Akil: "Don't Know If We've Turned That Corner" – TCA|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=de Moraes|first=Lisa|date=January 7, 2018|access-date=May 31, 2019|archive-date=June 4, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190604051255/https://deadline.com/2018/01/black-lightning-salim-akil-dc-comic-black-voices-tv-turned-corner-tca-1202237371/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="VT">{{cite web|url=https://variety.com/2018/tv/news/black-lightning-salim-akil-african-american-paranoia-community-based-superhero-1202657820/|title='Black Lightning' Boss on Telling a Tale of 'African-American Paranoia'|website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|last=Turchiano|first=Danielle|date=January 16, 2018|access-date=May 25, 2019|archive-date=June 16, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180616100640/https://variety.com/2018/tv/news/black-lightning-salim-akil-african-american-paranoia-community-based-superhero-1202657820/|url-status=live}}</ref> In writing the first season, showrunner Akil stated that he was most inspired by the original run of ''Black Lightning'' comic books and that Black Lightning being a black father who defies the "deadbeat stereotype" was part of the reason for the Akils wanting to tell his story.<ref name="IBT">{{cite web|url=http://www.ibtimes.com/black-lightning-tv-show-spoilers-what-eps-revealed-atx-2550641|title='Black Lightning' TV Show Spoilers: What The EPs Revealed At ATX|website=[[International Business Times]]|last=Massabrook|first=Nicole|date=June 11, 2017|access-date=July 17, 2017|archive-date=July 15, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170715222302/http://www.ibtimes.com/black-lightning-tv-show-spoilers-what-eps-revealed-atx-2550641|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="EW">{{cite magazine|url=https://ew.com/comic-con/2017/07/12/black-lightning-salim-akil-spoilers/|title=Black Lightning boss: 'This is an American story, this is not a black story'|magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]|last=Abrams|first=Natalie|date=July 12, 2017|access-date=May 25, 2019|archive-date=April 16, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190416072516/https://ew.com/comic-con/2017/07/12/black-lightning-salim-akil-spoilers/|url-status=live}}</ref> He described Jefferson and his family as "the [[Family of Barack Obama|Obamas]] of the superhero world" and compared the duality of Jefferson Pierce and his [[alter ego]] Black Lightning to the duality of [[Martin Luther King Jr.]] and [[Malcolm X]].<ref name="EW" /> As a character-driven family drama, ''Black Lightning'' does not follow a [[villain of the week]] format in order to better explore the characters, especially the villains. The Akils also indicated that the writers would not be treating [[LGBTQ]] representation as a "special issue" but that such characters would be included and depicted "the way anyone would be included in life."<ref name="IBT" /> Salim Akil noted that topics such as the [[Black Lives Matter]] movement and other issues concerning race relations and police brutality would be addressed, but stressed that, "This is an American story, this is not a black story. We're going to be culturally specific, but universal in our themes so everyone can see themselves in these stories."<ref name="EW" /> The showrunner likened the narrative of the first season to the real story of the [[Tuskegee experiment]].<ref name="VT" />

The second season is organized into smaller arcs known as "books" to mimic the style of the comic book source material, with "consequences" being the theme of the season's first book. Specifically, Salim Akil said that the season would "deal with the consequences of having discovered the pod children; the consequences of Green Light hitting the streets; and the consequences of Jefferson's daughters discovering they have powers."<ref name="Collider">{{cite web|url=https://collider.com/black-lightning-season-2-salim-akil-interview/|title='Black Lightning' Showrunner Salim Akil on Season 2 and the Story's Social Relevance|website=[[Collider (website)|Collider]]|last=Radish|first=Christina|date=September 26, 2018|access-date=November 3, 2018|archive-date=November 4, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181104125848/http://collider.com/black-lightning-season-2-salim-akil-interview/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.tvline.com/gallery/fall-tv-2018-season-premiere-spoilers/|title=Fall TV Spoilers 2018: Scoop on 40 Returning Favorites|website=[[TVLine]]|date=September 5, 2018 |access-date=March 20, 2019|archive-date=September 6, 2018|archive-url=https://archive.today/20180906172627/https://tvline.com/gallery/fall-tv-2018-season-premiere-spoilers/%23!15/undefined/#!4/undefined/|url-status=live}}</ref> Furthering the season's objective to "give a nod to comic books in a stronger way," the season introduces more metahumans, though showrunner Akil commented, "I don't want to introduce too many villains. I want us to settle in now that we know everyone [...] so now we can really tell some grounded stories about our villains, our heroes, the people in Freeland." He said that there would additionally be "other forces in Freeland and outside of Freeland" that would come into play as sources of conflict.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://comicbook.com/2018/07/31/black-lightning-showrunner-teases-more-supervillains-/|title='Black Lightning' Showrunner Hints At More Metahumans in Season 2|website=ComicBook.com|last=Burlingame|first=Russ|date=July 30, 2018|access-date=November 3, 2018|archive-date=August 2, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180802110533/http://comicbook.com/2018/07/31/black-lightning-showrunner-teases-more-supervillains-/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/black-lightning-season-2-details-dc-tv-watch-1142711|title='Black Lightning' Season 2: All the Details (So Far)|website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|last=Bucksbaum|first=Sydney|date=September 15, 2018|access-date=November 3, 2018|archive-date=October 8, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181008022738/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/black-lightning-season-2-details-dc-tv-watch-1142711|url-status=live}}</ref> Lead actor [[Cress Williams]] described the season as "harder hitting and a little bit darker" than the series' debut outing.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://fandomwire.com/2018/04/29/exclusive-black-lightning-star-talks-season-2-dc-crossovers/|title=EXCLUSIVE: 'Black Lightning' Star Talks Season 2 & DC Crossovers|website=Fandom Wire|last=Johnson|first=Reilly|date=April 29, 2018|access-date=April 7, 2019|archive-date=April 7, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190407183721/https://fandomwire.com/2018/04/29/exclusive-black-lightning-star-talks-season-2-dc-crossovers/|url-status=live}}</ref> On the relevant social issues that the season would address, Akil stated, "I wanted to talk about black people and therapy. We don't believe in that shit, but we're the number one people who need it."<ref name="Collider"/> Meanwhile, [[Nafessa Williams]] shared that her character would continue to embrace her powers, elaborating that Anissa now "feels confident navigating the superhero world without her father, and she feels fully confident and able to do it on her own."<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.yahoo.com/lifestyle/nafessa-williams-tvs-first-black-lesbian-superhero-talks-black-lightning-season-2-212022251.html|title=Nafessa Williams, TV's first black lesbian superhero, talks 'Black Lightning' Season 2|website=[[Yahoo!]]|last=Sarachan|first=Risa|date=October 8, 2018|access-date=April 20, 2019|archive-date=April 20, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190420234858/https://www.yahoo.com/lifestyle/nafessa-williams-tvs-first-black-lesbian-superhero-talks-black-lightning-season-2-212022251.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

The third season's narrative begins approximately a month and a half after the season two finale.<ref name="SAA">{{Cite web|url=https://shadowandact.com/how-black-lightning-season-3-will-be-more-apocalyptic-than-ever-before|title=How 'Black Lightning' Season 3 Will Be More Apocalyptic Than Ever Before|website=[[Shadow and Act]]|last=B|first=Kay|date=August 1, 2019|access-date=August 12, 2019|archive-date=August 11, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190811212549/https://shadowandact.com/how-black-lightning-season-3-will-be-more-apocalyptic-than-ever-before|url-status=live}}</ref> Cress Williams shared that the season would see the world of the series "getting bigger" in terms of its setting and characters.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://comicbook.com/dc/2019/07/20/black-lightning-more-superheroes-supervillains-coming-in-season-/|title=Black Lightning: More Superheroes, Supervillains Coming in Season Three|website=ComicBook.com|last=Burlingame|first=Russ|date=July 20, 2019|access-date=August 6, 2019|archive-date=August 7, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190807060141/https://comicbook.com/dc/2019/07/20/black-lightning-more-superheroes-supervillains-coming-in-season-/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/ustv/a28461818/black-lightning-season-3-outsiders-rumour/|title=Black Lightning star hints major DC superhero team could join show|website=[[Digital Spy]]|last=Sandwell|first=Ian|date=July 22, 2019|access-date=July 24, 2019|archive-date=July 24, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190724215133/https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/ustv/a28461818/black-lightning-season-3-outsiders-rumour/|url-status=live}}</ref> Salim Akil stated that, while everyday life in Freeland would still be a focus of the season, "we want our stories to talk about concerns not just for black folk but for people in general. We'll cover mental health and addiction issues that affect the whole country."<ref name="TVI">{{Cite web|url=https://www.tvinsider.com/806849/black-lightning-season-3-burning-questions-answered/|title='Black Lightning' Season 3: All Your Burning Questions Answered|website=[[TV Insider]]|last=Rudolph|first=Ileane|date=September 1, 2019|access-date=September 1, 2019|archive-date=October 17, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191017220401/https://www.tvinsider.com/806849/black-lightning-season-3-burning-questions-answered/|url-status=live}}</ref> Discussing Jennifer's ongoing struggle to control her newly discovered abilities, actress [[China Anne McClain]] noted that, "When the season starts, we see that Jennifer is getting more powerful, stronger, and she's also getting more emotional. We can expect a combination of all three of those this season."<ref name="SAA" /> Akil additionally disclosed that Jennifer being stronger than both her father and her sister on account of her unique ability to generate her own electricity would also raise the issue of who is ultimately in control amongst the three.<ref name="TVI" /> Meanwhile, Nafessa Williams said of her character Anissa's journey, "Season one was about her understanding and discovering her powers, in season two she is kind of starting to perfect them and trust herself. Season three, [...] her ways of doing things and her mindset is different from her father's."<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://meaww.com/sdcc-2019-san-diego-comic-con-50-tease-season-3-black-lightning-cress-williams-nafessa-china-mcclain|title=SDCC 2019: Black Lightning's Cress Williams says family disjointed when s3 begins, actors explain their upcoming arcs [EXCLUSIVE]|website=MEAWW|last=Sundar|first=Priyanka|date=July 20, 2019|access-date=September 3, 2019|archive-date=July 21, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190721030057/https://meaww.com/sdcc-2019-san-diego-comic-con-50-tease-season-3-black-lightning-cress-williams-nafessa-china-mcclain|url-status=live}}</ref> Furthermore, Williams teased that Jefferson would be making "a really big sacrifice" this season that would reveal "a little bit more of his angrier side" and "[propel] him at the beginning of the season."<ref>{{Cite magazine|url=https://ew.com/tv/2019/09/13/black-lightning-season-3-preview-cress-williams-markovia/|title=Black Lightning star teases Jefferson's 'big sacrifice' in the Markovian conflict|magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]|last=Agard|first=Chancellor|date=September 13, 2019|access-date=September 14, 2019|archive-date=September 21, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190921132127/https://ew.com/tv/2019/09/13/black-lightning-season-3-preview-cress-williams-markovia/|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Casting===
On February 24, 2017, [[Cress Williams]] was announced in the lead role of [[Black Lightning|Jefferson Pierce / Black Lightning]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://tvline.com/2017/02/24/black-lightning-cast-cress-williams-the-cw-dc-comics-pilot/|title=Black Lightning: Cress Williams to Star in The CW's Latest DC Comics Pilot|website=[[TVLine]]|last=Swift|first=Andy|date=February 24, 2017|access-date=February 24, 2017|archive-date=February 25, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170225051722/http://tvline.com/2017/02/24/black-lightning-cast-cress-williams-the-cw-dc-comics-pilot/|url-status=dead}}</ref> On March 2, [[China Anne McClain]] and [[Nafessa Williams]] were cast as Jefferson's daughters, [[Lightning (DC Comics)|Jennifer Pierce]] and [[Thunder (DC Comics)|Anissa Pierce]], respectively.<ref name="McClainWilliams" /> Later that same month on March 10, it was reported that [[Christine Adams (actress)|Christine Adams]] has been cast as Lynn Stewart, Jefferson's ex-wife.<ref name="Adams">{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2017/03/black-lightning-christine-adams-cast-jeffersons-ex-wife-lynn-the-cw-pilot-1202041455/|title='Black Lightning': Christine Adams Cast As Jefferson's Ex-Wife|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Andreeva|first=Nellie|date=March 10, 2017|access-date=May 10, 2017|archive-date=May 16, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170516091950/http://deadline.com/2017/03/black-lightning-christine-adams-cast-jeffersons-ex-wife-lynn-the-cw-pilot-1202041455/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://wegotthiscovered.com/tv/black-lightning-adds-christine-adams-lynn-stewart/|title=Black Lightning Adds Christine Adams As Lynn Stewart|website=We Got This Covered|last=Cassidy|first=Mark|date=March 10, 2017|access-date=April 26, 2019|archive-date=April 28, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190428050946/https://wegotthiscovered.com/tv/black-lightning-adds-christine-adams-lynn-stewart/|url-status=live}}</ref> At the 2017 [[San Diego Comic-Con]] on July 22, it was revealed that [[James Remar]] and [[Damon Gupton]] had joined the main cast as Jefferson's oldest friend [[Peter Gambi]] and unlikely ally [[Inspector Henderson|Inspector William "Bill" Henderson]], respectively.<ref name="RemarGupton" /><ref>{{cite web|url=https://comicbook.com/dc/2018/01/16/black-lightning-who-is-inspector-henderson-superman/|title='Black Lightning': Who Is Inspector Henderson?|website=ComicBook.com|last=Anderson|first=Jenna|date=January 16, 2018|access-date=April 27, 2019|archive-date=April 28, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190428050939/https://comicbook.com/dc/2018/01/16/black-lightning-who-is-inspector-henderson-superman/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.cbr.com/black-lightning-henderson-secret-identity/|title=Black Lightning: A Major Cast Member Learns His Secret Identity|website=[[Comic Book Resources|CBR]]|last=Adams|first=Tim|date=October 9, 2018|access-date=April 27, 2019|archive-date=April 28, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190428061628/https://www.cbr.com/black-lightning-henderson-secret-identity/|url-status=live}}</ref> On August 10, rapper [[Krondon|Marvin "Krondon" Jones III]] was added as a series regular, landing the role of main antagonist [[Tobias Whale]].<ref name="Jones">{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2017/08/marvin-krondon-jones-iii-black-lightning-tobias-whale-warner-brothers-tv-sam-akil-mara-brock-akil-the-cw-1202146162/|title='Black Lightning' Adds Marvin "Krondon" Jones III As Villain Tobias Whale|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Ramos|first=Dino-Ray|date=August 10, 2017|access-date=August 10, 2017|archive-date=August 11, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170811054943/http://deadline.com/2017/08/marvin-krondon-jones-iii-black-lightning-tobias-whale-warner-brothers-tv-sam-akil-mara-brock-akil-the-cw-1202146162/|url-status=live}}</ref> At the 2018 San Diego Comic-Con on July 21, it was announced that [[Jordan Calloway]] had been promoted to a series regular for the second season after previously recurring during the first season as [[Painkiller (comics)|Khalil Payne / Painkiller]].<ref name="Calloway">{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2018/07/black-lightning-jordan-calloway-painkiller-series-regular-season-2-comic-con-1202430769/|title='Black Lightning': Jordan Calloway Upped To Series Regular As Painkiller – Watch The Comic-Con Sizzle Reel|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|first1=Amanda|last1=N'Duka|date=July 21, 2018|access-date=October 7, 2018|archive-date=October 8, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181008022742/https://deadline.com/2018/07/black-lightning-jordan-calloway-painkiller-series-regular-season-2-comic-con-1202430769/|url-status=live}}</ref>

On September 26, 2017, it was announced that [[Kyanna Simone Simpson]] would recur as Kiesha, Henderson's daughter and Jennifer's best friend.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2017/09/black-lightning-kyanna-simone-simpson-recur-cw-series-1202176356/|title='Black Lightning': Kyanna Simone Simpson Set To Recur In the CW Series|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Petski|first=Denise|date=September 26, 2017|access-date=September 27, 2017|archive-date=September 26, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170926222616/http://deadline.com/2017/09/black-lightning-kyanna-simone-simpson-recur-cw-series-1202176356/|url-status=live}}</ref> On October 5, it was reported that [[Jill Scott (singer)|Jill Scott]] had been cast as [[Lady Eve (comics)|Lady Eve]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2017/10/black-lightning-jill-scott-cast-lady-eve-cw-series-1202182537/|title='Black Lightning': Jill Scott Cast As Lady Eve In the CW Series|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Petski|first=Denise|date=October 5, 2017|access-date=April 27, 2019|archive-date=April 28, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190428050942/https://deadline.com/2017/10/black-lightning-jill-scott-cast-lady-eve-cw-series-1202182537/|url-status=live}}</ref> Later that month on October 12, [[Edwina Findley]] also joined the cast in a recurring capacity as Tori Whale, Tobias' younger sister.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2017/10/black-lightning-edwina-findley-recur-the-cw-series-1202187033/|title='Black Lightning': Edwina Findley Set To Recur In the CW Series|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Petski|first=Denise|date=October 12, 2017|access-date=November 1, 2017|archive-date=November 1, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171101230810/http://deadline.com/2017/10/black-lightning-edwina-findley-recur-the-cw-series-1202187033/|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Chantal Thuy]] was added to the recurring cast as [[Grace Choi]] that same month on October 30,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://variety.com/2017/tv/news/black-lightning-chantal-thuy-dc-comics-grace-choi-exclusive-1202602693/|title='Black Lightning' Casts Chantal Thuy as DC Comics' Grace Choi (Exclusive)|website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|last=Bryant|first=Jacob|date=October 30, 2017|access-date=October 30, 2017|archive-date=October 30, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171030234226/http://variety.com/2017/tv/news/black-lightning-chantal-thuy-dc-comics-grace-choi-exclusive-1202602693/|url-status=live}}</ref> though she ultimately appeared in only two episodes of the series' first season.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.pastemagazine.com/tv/black-lightning/black-lightning-season-one-finale-the-cw|title=Our Only Complaint About Black Lightning: We Wish There Were More of It|website=[[Paste (magazine)|Paste]]|last=Gunderson|first=Alexis|date=April 17, 2018|access-date=April 27, 2019|archive-date=March 31, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190331043001/https://www.pastemagazine.com/articles/2018/04/black-lightning-season-one-finale-the-cw.html|url-status=live}}</ref> On January 16, 2018, it was revealed that Skye P. Marshall had been cast in a recurring role as Kara Fowdy, the vice principal of Garfield High School.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2018/01/black-lightning-skye-marshall-recur-the-cw-series-1202244242/|title='Black Lightning': Skye Marshall To Recur On the CW Series|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Petski|first=Denise|date=January 16, 2018|access-date=April 20, 2019|archive-date=March 23, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190323073551/https://deadline.com/2018/01/black-lightning-skye-marshall-recur-the-cw-series-1202244242/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://bestofcomicbooks.com/skye-marshall-butt-kara-fowdy-bootyfacts-black-lightning/|title=7 Lesser Known Facts About Skye P Marshall Who Plays Kara Fowdy In Black Lightning TV Show.|website=Best of Comic Books|author=Ash|date=April 22, 2018|access-date=April 27, 2019|archive-date=April 28, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190428050950/https://bestofcomicbooks.com/skye-marshall-butt-kara-fowdy-bootyfacts-black-lightning/|url-status=live}}</ref>

On August 8, 2018, it was reported that [[Myles Truitt]] would play Issa Williams during the second season in a recurring capacity.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://shadowandact.com/myles-truitt-joins-black-lightning-season-2|title=Myles Truitt Joins 'Black Lightning' Season 2|website=Shadow and Act|last=Mangum|first=Trey|date=August 8, 2018|access-date=March 22, 2019|archive-date=March 23, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190323073550/https://shadowandact.com/myles-truitt-joins-black-lightning-season-2|url-status=live}}</ref> On September 5, [[Sofia Vassilieva]] was announced in the role of [[Looker (character)|Looker]], based on the [[DC Comics]] character of the same name.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://tvline.com/2018/09/05/black-lightning-season-2-casts-looker-sofia-vassilieva/|title=Black Lightning Season 2 Casts Supergirl Foil as DC Comics' Looker|website=[[TVLine]]|last=Mitovich|first=Matt Webb|date=September 5, 2018|access-date=October 7, 2018|archive-date=October 23, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181023024222/https://tvline.com/2018/09/05/black-lightning-season-2-casts-looker-sofia-vassilieva/|url-status=dead}}</ref> On September 21, it was reported that [[Kearran Giovanni]] would recur as Cutter, a British mercenary.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2018/09/black-lightning-kearran-giovannia-recur-season-2-cw-series-1202469335/|title='Black Lightning': Kearran Giovanni To Recur On Season 2 Of CW Series|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Petski|first=Denise|date=September 21, 2018|access-date=October 7, 2018|archive-date=September 22, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180922112650/https://deadline.com/2018/09/black-lightning-kearran-giovannia-recur-season-2-cw-series-1202469335/|url-status=live}}</ref> On October 4, it was revealed that [[Erika Alexander]] had booked a three-episode recurring role as Jennifer's telepathic therapist, Perenna,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/black-lightning-casts-erika-alexander-perenna-therapist-season-2-987681/|title=Black Lightning Casts Living Single Vet as [Spoiler]'s Super-Powered Therapist|website=[[TVLine]]|last=Gelman|first=Vlada|date=October 4, 2018|access-date=October 7, 2018|archive-date=October 8, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181008022740/https://tvline.com/2018/10/04/black-lightning-casts-erika-alexander-perenna-therapist-season-2/|url-status=live}}</ref> though she ultimately appeared in a total of eight episodes. [[Robert Townsend (actor)|Robert Townsend]] and [[Bill Duke]] were added as recurring characters Dr. Napier Frank and Agent Percy Odell, respectively, on October 9.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://shadowandact.com/robert-townsend-and-bill-duke-join-black-lightning-season-2|title=Robert Townsend And Bill Duke Join 'Black Lightning' Season 2|website=Shadow and Act|last=Mangum|first=Trey|date=October 9, 2018|access-date=March 22, 2019|archive-date=March 23, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190323073733/https://shadowandact.com/robert-townsend-and-bill-duke-join-black-lightning-season-2|url-status=live}}</ref> On November 13, [[RJ Cyler]] was cast in the recurring role of "gangly and awkward tech genius" Todd Green.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2018/11/black-lightning-casts-rj-cyler-antonio-jaramillo-seal-team-1202500782/|title='Black Lightning' Casts RJ Cyler; Antonio Jaramillo Joins 'SEAL Team'|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Petski|first=Denise|date=November 13, 2018|access-date=November 13, 2018|archive-date=November 13, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181113231935/https://deadline.com/2018/11/black-lightning-casts-rj-cyler-antonio-jaramillo-seal-team-1202500782/|url-status=live}}</ref> On January 21, 2019, it was announced that [[Hosea Chanchez]] had been cast to recur as [[Shakedown (comics)|Marcus Bishop / Shakedown]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2019/01/black-lightning-hosea-chanchez-recur-season-2-cw-series-1202538601/|title='Black Lightning': Hosea Chanchez To Recur On Season 2 Of CW Series|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Petski|first=Denise|date=January 21, 2019|access-date=January 21, 2019|archive-date=January 24, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190124092028/https://deadline.com/2019/01/black-lightning-hosea-chanchez-recur-season-2-cw-series-1202538601/|url-status=live}}</ref>

On October 10, 2019, it was announced that [[Wayne Brady]] would recur during the third season as [[Gravedigger (comics)|Tyson Sykes / Gravedigger]], a World War II-era "super soldier" and American-turned-Markovian asset.<ref name="Brady">{{cite web|url=https://www.etonline.com/wayne-brady-joins-black-lightning-as-gravedigger-exclusive-134127|title=Wayne Brady Joins 'Black Lightning' as Gravedigger (Exclusive)|website=[[Entertainment Tonight]]|last1=Ng|first1=Philiana|last2=Seemayer|first2=Zach|date=October 10, 2019|access-date=October 10, 2019|archive-date=October 10, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191010215034/https://www.etonline.com/wayne-brady-joins-black-lightning-as-gravedigger-exclusive-134127|url-status=live}}</ref> On January 19, 2020, Gupton revealed that he had been let go from the series and that the third season would be his last as a series regular.<ref name="GuptonExit">{{cite web|url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/black-lightning-damon-gupton-leaving-season-4-chief-henderson-1148138/|title=Black Lightning: Original Cast Member Damon Gupton Out Ahead of Season 4|website=[[TVLine]]|last=Mitovich|first=Matt Webb|date=January 19, 2020|access-date=January 19, 2020|archive-date=January 20, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200120115526/https://tvline.com/2020/01/19/black-lightning-damon-gupton-leaving-season-4-chief-henderson/|url-status=live}}</ref> On November 13, 2020, [[Chantal Thuy]] was promoted to a series regular for the fourth season.<ref name="ChantalTPromoted">{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2020/11/black-lightning-chantal-thuy-series-regular-the-cw-season-4-asian-american-superhero-grace-choi-ryan-choi-1234613659/|title='Black Lightning' Ups Chantal Thuy To Series Regular; Actress Talks Season 4, Asian And LGBTQ Representation In The Superhero Genre|website=Deadline Hollywood|first=Dino-Ray|last=Ramos|date=November 13, 2020|access-date=November 13, 2020|archive-date=November 13, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201113173136/https://deadline.com/2020/11/black-lightning-chantal-thuy-series-regular-the-cw-season-4-asian-american-superhero-grace-choi-ryan-choi-1234613659/|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Design===
Black Lightning's costume was designed by Laura Jean Shannon.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2017/03/29/first-look-at-black-lightning-from-the-cws-new-dc-comics-pilot|title=First Look At Black Lightning From The CW's New DC Comics Pilot|website=[[IGN]]|last=Goldman|first=Eric|date=March 29, 2017|access-date=March 30, 2017|archive-date=March 29, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170329234146/http://www.ign.com/articles/2017/03/29/first-look-at-black-lightning-from-the-cws-new-dc-comics-pilot|url-status=live}}</ref> While the suit's design is meant to invoke protection from the character's vulnerabilities such as his age, and bullets in particular, Salim Akil stated that there were "a lot of iterations" of the Black Lightning costume, and that "at one point I had covered his face and his eyes, but what was more important to me was the emotion, and you need to see that. You need to see his eyes when his daughters have a gun pointed at them."<ref name="VT" /><ref name="EW" /> A number of journalists noted similarities between the first superhero costume donned by Anissa Pierce, featuring a pink, purple, and blue color scheme with gold and black accents and a blonde wig, and the Thunder costume of the 2003 ''[[Outsiders (comics)|Outsiders]]'' comic book run.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.cbr.com/black-lightning-outsiders-costume-anissa/|title=Black Lightning: [SPOILER] Dons Comics-Accurate Outsiders Costume|website=[[Comic Book Resources|CBR]]|last=Damore|first=Meagan|date=February 13, 2018|access-date=April 21, 2019|archive-date=April 21, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190421192956/https://www.cbr.com/black-lightning-outsiders-costume-anissa/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://comicbook.com/dc/2018/04/25/7-best-moments-in-black-lightnings-first-season/|title=7 Best Moments in 'Black Lightning's First Season|website=ComicBook.com|last=Drum|first=Nicole|date=April 24, 2018|access-date=June 3, 2019|archive-date=June 4, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190604051253/https://comicbook.com/dc/2018/04/25/7-best-moments-in-black-lightnings-first-season/|url-status=live}}</ref> Shannon also designed the final Thunder costume, which was made from a sculpted armor material in order to stretch to the performer's comfort and serves as an homage to the most recent costume worn by Thunder in the comic books.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://ew.com/tv/2018/03/20/black-lightning-nafessa-williams-cried-thunder-suit/|title=Black Lightning: Why Nafessa Williams cried the first time she wore Thunder's suit|magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]|last=Goldman|first=Eric|date=March 20, 2018|access-date=April 21, 2019|archive-date=April 21, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190421192955/https://ew.com/tv/2018/03/20/black-lightning-nafessa-williams-cried-thunder-suit/|url-status=live}}</ref> The second season introduces the first official superhero costume for Jennifer Pierce as she takes on the moniker "Lightning" from the comic book source material. The costume echoes that of Anissa Pierce, in that it is a black body suit covered in yellow plating. However, the Lightning costume also features lightning-inspired designs.<ref name="Lightning">{{Cite web|url=https://www.cbr.com/black-lightning-unveils-first-look-at-mcclains-lightning-costume/|title=Black Lightning Unveils First Look at McClain's Lightning Costume|website=[[Comic Book Resources|CBR]]|last=Damore|first=Meagan|date=December 13, 2018|access-date=March 18, 2019|archive-date=December 14, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181214113630/https://www.cbr.com/black-lightning-unveils-first-look-at-mcclains-lightning-costume/|url-status=live}}</ref> The third season features a new suit design for Jefferson Pierce as Black Lightning. In place of the previous suit's glowing blue and gold bolts across the chest, a textured gold design with blue and black weaving is featured throughout the torso, arms, and gloves. The mask is also slightly redesigned with dark red-tinted lenses.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://comicbook.com/2019/09/21/black-lightning-new-costume-leaked-photo-season-3/|title=Black Lightning Gets New Costume in Leaked Photo From Season 3|website=ComicBook.com|last=Aguilar|first=Matthew|date=September 20, 2019|access-date=September 24, 2019|archive-date=June 12, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210612120540/https://comicbook.com/dc/news/black-lightning-new-costume-leaked-photo-season-3/|url-status=live}}</ref> As Anissa Pierce officially takes on the name "Blackbird" as a second secret identity, she also receives a new costume for the alter-ego that consists of a black hood and a mask that covers the lower half of her face.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://meaww.com/black-lightning-season-3-cw-anissa-pierce-nafessa-williams-blackbird-thunder-grace-choi|title=Anissa's new Blackbird identity in 'Black Lightning' Season 3 is a sign that she's ready to step out of her father's shadow|website=MEAWW|last=Noronha|first=Remus|date=September 25, 2019|access-date=September 26, 2019|archive-date=September 26, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190926192551/https://meaww.com/black-lightning-season-3-cw-anissa-pierce-nafessa-williams-blackbird-thunder-grace-choi|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Filming===
Filming for the series takes place in [[Decatur, Georgia|Decatur]], [[Georgia (U.S. state)|Georgia]] and the surrounding [[Atlanta]] area.<ref name="Premise" /><ref>{{cite web|url=https://shadowandact.com/the-women-of-black-lightning-on-being-badass-embracing-their-powers-in-the-high-stakes-season-2|title=The Women Of 'Black Lightning' On Being Badass, Embracing Their Powers In The 'High Stakes' Season 2|website=[[Shadow and Act]]|last=Tinubu|first=Aramide A.|date=October 24, 2018|access-date=August 10, 2019|archive-date=August 11, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190811024230/https://shadowandact.com/the-women-of-black-lightning-on-being-badass-embracing-their-powers-in-the-high-stakes-season-2|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2017/03/pilot-locations-2017-new-york-vancouver-atlanta-los-angeles-toronto-chicago-1202035016/|title=Pilot Locations 2017: NY, Vancouver & Atlanta Tick Up; LA, Toronto, Chicago Slip|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Andreeva|first=Nellie|date=March 7, 2017|access-date=May 11, 2017|archive-date=July 28, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170728134236/http://deadline.com/2017/03/pilot-locations-2017-new-york-vancouver-atlanta-los-angeles-toronto-chicago-1202035016/|url-status=live}}</ref> The short presentation that was given to The CW was filmed in March 2017,<ref name="BLCostume">{{Cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2017/03/black-lightning-pilot-first-look-image-cress-williams-the-cw-1202055072/|title='Black Lightning' Pilot: First-Look Image Of Cress Williams As Title Character|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Petski|first=Denise|date=March 29, 2017|access-date=April 14, 2019|archive-date=April 14, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190414171727/https://deadline.com/2017/03/black-lightning-pilot-first-look-image-cress-williams-the-cw-1202055072/|url-status=live}}</ref> with production for the series officially commencing on September 7, 2017.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.instagram.com/maraakil/p/BYv2giahG2q/|title=...In honor of our #firstday of principal photography for #BLACKLIGHTNING...|via=[[Instagram]]|last=Bella|first=Mara|date=September 7, 2017|access-date=April 23, 2019}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.instagram.com/p/BYwAX3NBiyG/ |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/iarchive/s/instagram/BYwAX3NBiyG |archive-date=December 26, 2021 |url-access=registration|title=And the journey begins. Day 1. # Black Lightning|via=[[Instagram]]|last=Adams|first=Christine|date=September 7, 2017|access-date=April 23, 2019}}{{cbignore}}</ref> Filming for the first season concluded on March 3, 2018.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.instagram.com/p/Bf3QecShF-L/ |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/iarchive/s/instagram/Bf3QecShF-L |archive-date=December 26, 2021 |url-access=registration|title=Season 1. That's a wrap! Goodbye for now Lynn Stewart...|via=[[Instagram]]|last=Adams|first=Christine|date=March 3, 2018|access-date=April 21, 2019}}{{cbignore}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.instagram.com/p/Bf3EX6fjwgS/ |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/iarchive/s/instagram/Bf3EX6fjwgS |archive-date=December 26, 2021 |url-access=registration|title=That's a wrap on Season 1 of #BlackLightning...|via=[[Instagram]]|last=Williams|first=Nafessa|date=March 3, 2017|access-date=April 21, 2019}}{{cbignore}}</ref> Production for the second season returned to Atlanta beginning on June 26, 2018.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://comicbook.com/dc/2018/06/28/black-lightning-season-2-production-begins/|title='Black Lightning' Season 2 Has Begun Production|website=ComicBook.com|last=Drum|first=Nicole|date=June 28, 2018|access-date=October 7, 2018|archive-date=October 8, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181008061300/https://comicbook.com/dc/2018/06/28/black-lightning-season-2-production-begins/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.11alive.com/mobile/article/entertainment/television/programs/the-a-scene/whats-filming-in-atlanta-the-second-week-of-september/85-592467463|title=What's filming in Atlanta the second week of September!|website=WXIA|date=September 10, 2018|access-date=October 8, 2018}}</ref> The back lot used during filming was the same one used by The CW's previous Atlanta-based television series, ''[[The Vampire Diaries]]''.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://tonyisabella.blogspot.com/2019/02/tony-goes-to-freeland-part-four.html?m=1|title=Tony Goes To Freeland: Part Four|website=Tony Isabella's Bloggy Thing|last=Isabella|first=Tony|date=February 27, 2018|access-date=March 20, 2019|archive-date=June 12, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210612120526/https://tonyisabella.blogspot.com/2019/02/tony-goes-to-freeland-part-four.html?m=1|url-status=live}}</ref> Filming for the second season concluded on January 10, 2019.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.instagram.com/p/BsesB4sn4dc/ |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/iarchive/s/instagram/BsesB4sn4dc |archive-date=December 26, 2021 |url-access=registration|title=We just filmed our last scene for Season 2...|via=[[Instagram]]|last=Williams|first=Nafessa|date=January 10, 2019|access-date=March 18, 2019}}{{cbignore}}</ref> Production for the third season began on July 9, 2019.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.instagram.com/p/BztwGQOFTrw/|title=First day Mood #BlackLightning #Season3 😛⚡️💃🏻|via=[[Instagram]]|last=Williams|first=Nafessa|date=July 9, 2019|access-date=July 12, 2019}}</ref> A week was carved out of the season's production for Williams to film his scenes for the [[Arrowverse]] crossover event "[[Crisis on Infinite Earths (Arrowverse)|Crisis on Infinite Earths]]" in [[Vancouver, British Columbia]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://variety.com/2019/tv/features/arrowverse-boss-breaks-down-journey-to-crisis-on-infinite-earths-1203426800/|title='Arrowverse' Boss Breaks Down Journey to 'Crisis on Infinite Earths'|website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|last=Roffman|first=Marisa|date=December 5, 2019|access-date=December 15, 2019|archive-date=December 6, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191206034801/https://variety.com/2019/tv/features/arrowverse-boss-breaks-down-journey-to-crisis-on-infinite-earths-1203426800/|url-status=live}}</ref> Filming for the third season concluded on January 20, 2020.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.instagram.com/p/B7jt48Wlmer/ |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/iarchive/s/instagram/B7jt48Wlmer |archive-date=December 26, 2021 |url-access=registration|title=Just filmed my last scene for Season 3, it's a wrap for the kid ✌🏾 #BlackLightning|via=[[Instagram]]|last=Williams|first=Nafessa|date=January 20, 2020|access-date=January 20, 2020}}{{cbignore}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.instagram.com/p/B7j2jtLHOeY/ |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/iarchive/s/instagram/B7j2jtLHOeY |archive-date=December 26, 2021 |url-access=registration|title=There are no endings, only beginnings. Thats a picture wrap on season 3 @cw_blacklightning 🔥⚡️|via=[[Instagram]]|last=Adams|first=Christine|date=January 20, 2020|access-date=January 20, 2020}}{{cbignore}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.instagram.com/p/B7RC3RIl9Qa/ |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/iarchive/s/instagram/B7RC3RIl9Qa |archive-date=December 26, 2021 |url-access=registration|title=BLACK LIGHTNING// Headed to celebrate the success and wrap of #Season3 #BlackLightning...|via=[[Instagram]]|last=Akil|first=Mara|date=January 20, 2020|access-date=January 20, 2020}}{{cbignore}}</ref>

===Music===
[[Kurt Farquhar]] composes the score for the series and Kier Lehman, the music supervisor for ''Black Lightning'', selects the series' featured songs along with the Akils.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.awardsdaily.com/2018/02/08/composer-kurt-farquhar-interview/|title=Composer Kurt Farquhar on What Sets 'Black Lightning' Apart From Other Superhero Shows|website=[[Awards Daily]]|last=Haddad|first=Jalal|date=February 8, 2018|access-date=April 23, 2019|archive-date=April 23, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190423051844/http://www.awardsdaily.com/2018/02/08/composer-kurt-farquhar-interview/|url-status=live}}</ref> The rapper Godholly, who is the son of showrunner Akil, has provided original music for the series, including tracks such as "Black Lightning" from the main title sequence.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://variety.com/2018/tv/features/black-lightning-salim-akil-writers-office-art-inspiration-1202823213/|title='Black Lightning' Boss on How an Artful Life Inspires His Work|website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|last=Turchiano|first=Danielle|date=May 30, 2018|access-date=April 23, 2019|archive-date=April 27, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190427173150/https://variety.com/2018/tv/features/black-lightning-salim-akil-writers-office-art-inspiration-1202823213/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://andscape.com/features/behind-the-scenes-of-black-lightning-reveals-the-intersection-of-race-social-justice-and-culture/|title=Behind the scenes of 'Black Lightning' reveals the intersection of race, social justice and culture|website=[[Andscape]]|last=Thompson|first=Gianina|date=January 11, 2018|access-date=April 23, 2019|archive-date=April 23, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190423051852/http://theundefeated.com/features/behind-the-scenes-of-black-lightning-reveals-the-intersection-of-race-social-justice-and-culture/|url-status=live}}</ref>

==Release==
===Broadcast===
''Black Lightning'' began airing on [[The CW]] in the United States on January 16, 2018, during the [[2017–18 United States network television schedule|2017–18 television season]].<ref name="PremiereDate">{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2017/11/black-lightning-gets-premiere-date-post-flash-time-slot-by-the-cw-1202209913/|title='Black Lightning' Gets Premiere Date, Post-'Flash' Time Slot By the CW|last=Andreeva|first=Nellie|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|date=November 16, 2017|access-date=November 16, 2017|archive-date=November 16, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171116205410/http://deadline.com/2017/11/black-lightning-gets-premiere-date-post-flash-time-slot-by-the-cw-1202209913/|url-status=live}}</ref> The first season, consisting of 13 episodes, ran until April 17, 2018.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.pastemagazine.com/tv/black-lightning/black-lightning-season-one-finale-the-cw|title=Our Only Complaint About Black Lightning: We Wish There Were More of It|website=[[Paste (magazine)|Paste]]|last=Gunderson|first=Alexis|date=April 17, 2018|access-date=March 30, 2019|archive-date=March 31, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190331043001/https://www.pastemagazine.com/articles/2018/04/black-lightning-season-one-finale-the-cw.html|url-status=live}}</ref> The second season premiered on The CW in the United States on October 9, 2018.<ref name="Swift" /> In November, it was announced that the series would move to airing on Mondays for the second half of the season after previously airing on Tuesdays since its debut.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2018/11/the-cw-sets-midseason-schedule-roswell-new-mexico-gets-premiere-date-black-lightning-moves-monday-1202500213/|title=The CW Sets Midseason Schedule: 'Roswell, New Mexico' Gets Premiere Date, 'Black Lightning' Moves To Monday|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Petski|first=Denise|date=November 12, 2018|access-date=November 12, 2018|archive-date=November 12, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181112220929/https://deadline.com/2018/11/the-cw-sets-midseason-schedule-roswell-new-mexico-gets-premiere-date-black-lightning-moves-monday-1202500213/|url-status=live}}</ref> The 16th and final episode of the second season aired on March 18, 2019.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://comicbook.com/dc/2019/03/19/black-lightning-season-2-finale-breakdown-markovia/|title='Black Lightning': Breaking Down the Season 2 Finale Ending|website=ComicBook.com|last=Drum|first=Nicole|date=March 18, 2019|access-date=March 18, 2019|archive-date=March 19, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190319163807/https://comicbook.com/dc/2019/03/19/black-lightning-season-2-finale-breakdown-markovia/|url-status=live}}</ref> The third season premiered on October 7, 2019.<ref name="S3" /> The 16th and final episode of the third season aired on March 9, 2020.<ref name="EpCount">{{Cite tweet|number=1205627311875338240|title=Today we start episode 315! Wtf. One more episode left. This season flew by. Appreciate yall for riding with us. Alright bye, let me finish putting this suit on. #Thunder #BlackLightning ⚡️|user=NafessaWilliams|last=Williams|first=Nafessa|date=December 13, 2019|access-date=December 15, 2019}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2019/11/the-cw-midseason-premiere-dates-katy-keene-return-dcs-legends-roswell-new-mexico-supernatural-moves-to-monday-1202781471/|title=The CW Sets Midseason Premiere Dates: 'Katy Keene', Return Of 'DC's Legends', 'Roswell, New Mexico', 'Supernatural' Moves To Monday|last=Petski|first=Denise|date=November 8, 2019|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|access-date=November 8, 2019|archive-date=November 9, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191109083953/https://deadline.com/2019/11/the-cw-midseason-premiere-dates-katy-keene-return-dcs-legends-roswell-new-mexico-supernatural-moves-to-monday-1202781471/|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Home media===
Having acquired the international distribution and [[Streaming media|streaming]] rights for ''Black Lightning'', [[Netflix]] aired new episodes of the first two seasons weekly in regions outside of the United States, including [[Canada]], [[Australia]], [[New Zealand]], the [[United Kingdom]], [[Ireland]], most of mainland [[Europe]], and [[South America]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.whats-on-netflix.com/news/black-lightning-season-2-netflix-release-schedule/|title=Black Lightning Season 2 Netflix Release Schedule|website=What's on Netflix|last=Moore|first=Kasey|date=March 20, 2019|access-date=March 30, 2019|archive-date=October 2, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181002181129/https://www.whats-on-netflix.com/news/black-lightning-season-2-netflix-release-schedule/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://anz.newonnetflix.info/info/80178687|title=Info Page: Black Lightning|website=New on Netflix|access-date=July 7, 2019|archive-date=July 8, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190708170158/https://anz.newonnetflix.info/info/80178687|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2017/12/netflix-international-distribution-nbc-good-girls-star-trek-discovery-1202217186/|title=Netflix Inks Int'l Distribution Deal For NBC's 'Good Girls': Inside New Model That Partners the SVOD Giant With U.S. Studios|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Andreeva|first=Nellie|date=December 11, 2017|access-date=March 30, 2019|archive-date=December 12, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171212020654/http://deadline.com/2017/12/netflix-international-distribution-nbc-good-girls-star-trek-discovery-1202217186/|url-status=live}}</ref> However, following the expiration of the deal between the streamer and the network, the third season's released date on Netflix internationally was postponed.<ref name="NW">{{cite web|url=https://www.newsweek.com/black-lightning-season-3-netflix-release-date-when-series-streaming-1466639|title='Black Lightning' Season 3 Netflix Release Date: When is the Series Streaming?|website=[[Newsweek]]|last=Spencer|first=Samuel|date=October 21, 2019|access-date=December 13, 2019|archive-date=December 12, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191212233210/https://www.newsweek.com/black-lightning-season-3-netflix-release-date-when-series-streaming-1466639|url-status=live}}</ref> In the United States, the first season was released on Netflix in its entirety a week after the season finale aired on The CW.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://comicbook.com/dc/2018/04/25/black-lightning-season-1-streaming-netflix/|title='Black Lightning' Season 1 is Now on Netflix|website=ComicBook.com|last=Drum|first=Nicole|date=April 26, 2018|access-date=December 15, 2019|archive-date=April 14, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190414004702/https://comicbook.com/dc/2018/04/25/black-lightning-season-1-streaming-netflix/|url-status=live}}</ref> The second season was similarly released in its entirety on Netflix in the United States two weeks after the season finale aired on The CW.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://comicbook.com/dc/2019/04/02/black-lightning-season-2-netflix/|title='Black Lightning' Season 2 Is Now Available to Stream on Netflix|website=ComicBook.com|last=Drum|first=Nicole|date=April 1, 2019|access-date=December 15, 2019|archive-date=April 5, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190405015730/https://comicbook.com/dc/2019/04/02/black-lightning-season-2-netflix/|url-status=live}}</ref> The third season was released in its entirety on Netflix in the United States on March 17, 2020.<ref name="NW" />

The complete first season of ''Black Lightning'' was released on [[Blu-ray]] and [[DVD]] by [[Warner Home Entertainment]] in [[DVD region code#Region codes and countries|Region 1]] on June 26, 2018,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.amazon.com/Black-Lightning-China-Anne-McClain/dp/B07CDVZ479|title=Black Lightning: Season 1|website=[[Amazon (company)|Amazon]]|access-date=April 14, 2019|archive-date=April 14, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190414004701/https://www.amazon.com/Black-Lightning-China-Anne-McClain/dp/B07CDVZ479|url-status=live}}</ref> in [[DVD region code#Region codes and countries|Region 2]] on January 28, 2019,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.amazon.co.uk/Black-Lightning-Season-1-DVD/dp/B07JHX7YWZ/ref=sr_1_1_twi_dvd_2?ie=UTF8&qid=1551221098&sr=8-1&keywords=black+lightening+season+1|title=Black Lightning - Season 1|website=[[Amazon UK|Amazon]]|access-date=February 26, 2019|archive-date=June 12, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210612120542/https://www.amazon.co.uk/Black-Lightning-Season-1-DVD/dp/B07JHX7YWZ/ref=sr_1_1_twi_dvd_2?ie=UTF8&qid=1551221098&sr=8-1&keywords=black+lightening+season+1|url-status=live}}</ref> and in [[DVD region code#Region codes and countries|Region 4]] in 2018.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.buydvds.com.au/buy-australia-dvd/buy-black-lightning-season-1-dvd-in-australia/|title=Black Lightning: Season 1 (DVD AU)|website=Buy DVDs|access-date=September 3, 2018|archive-date=April 14, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190414034736/https://www.buydvds.com.au/buy-australia-dvd/buy-black-lightning-season-1-dvd-in-australia/|url-status=live}}</ref> The set also features extra content including the series' 2017 [[San Diego Comic-Con]] panel, new featurettes, deleted scenes, and a gag reel.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.tvinsider.com/698205/black-lightning-season-1-dvd-release/|title='Black Lightning' Season 1 DVD Includes Tons of Bonus Material (VIDEO)|website=[[TV Insider]]|last=Napoli|first=Jessica|date=June 22, 2018|access-date=April 14, 2019|archive-date=March 24, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190324184710/https://www.tvinsider.com/698205/black-lightning-season-1-dvd-release/|url-status=live}}</ref> The complete second season was made available as a [[Manufacture on demand|manufacture-on-demand]] DVD through the [[Warner Archive Collection]] on October 8, 2019.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.deepdiscount.com/black-lightning-the-complete-second-season/883929697496|title=Black Lightning: The Complete Second Season|website=Deep Discount|access-date=September 30, 2019|archive-date=June 12, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210612120544/https://www.deepdiscount.com/black-lightning-the-complete-second-season/883929697496|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.metacritic.com/feature/dvd-blu-ray-release-calendar-october-2019|title=DVD/Blu-ray Release Calendar: October 2019|website=[[Metacritic]]|last=Dietz|first=Jason|date=September 27, 2019|access-date=September 30, 2019|archive-date=September 30, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190930212758/https://www.metacritic.com/feature/dvd-blu-ray-release-calendar-october-2019|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Marketing===
On March 29, 2017, The CW released the first promotional image of [[Cress Williams]] as Jefferson Pierce in his official [[Black Lightning]] superhero costume.<ref name="BLCostume" /> On May 18, the first trailer for the series was released.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2017/05/the-cw-black-lightning-trailer-first-look-1202097203/|title='Black Lightning' Trailer: First Look At The CW's DC Comics Drama|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Petski|first=Denise|date=May 18, 2017|access-date=April 14, 2019|archive-date=April 14, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190414171734/https://deadline.com/2017/05/the-cw-black-lightning-trailer-first-look-1202097203/|url-status=live}}</ref> The main cast that were confirmed at the time, as well as [[executive producer]]s Salim Akil and [[Mara Brock Akil]] attended the 2017 San Diego Comic-Con on July 22 to promote the season.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2017/06/comic-con-warner-bros-tv-to-show-off-expanded-dc-universe-series-black-lightning-krypton-more-1202121954/|title=Comic-Con: Warner Bros. TV To Show Off Expanded DC Universe Series 'Black Lightning', 'Krypton' & More|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=D'Alessandro|first=Anthony|date=June 29, 2017|access-date=April 13, 2019|archive-date=April 14, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190414004701/https://deadline.com/2017/06/comic-con-warner-bros-tv-to-show-off-expanded-dc-universe-series-black-lightning-krypton-more-1202121954/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://variety.com/2017/tv/news/black-lightning-authentic-black-voice-comic-con-cw-1202503796/|title='Black Lightning' Cast and Crew Promise 'An Authentic Black Voice'|website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|last=Gordon|first=Diane|date=July 22, 2017|access-date=April 13, 2019|archive-date=April 26, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190426022308/https://variety.com/2017/tv/news/black-lightning-authentic-black-voice-comic-con-cw-1202503796/|url-status=live}}</ref> On December 12, The CW released key art for the series in the form of the season's first promotional poster featuring Williams, [[China Anne McClain]], and [[Nafessa Williams]] as their characters.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2017/12/black-lightning-cw-series-key-art-1202225236/|title='Black Lightning': CW Series' Key Art Unveiled|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Petski|first=Denise|date=December 12, 2017|access-date=April 14, 2019|archive-date=April 14, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190414171724/https://deadline.com/2017/12/black-lightning-cw-series-key-art-1202225236/|url-status=live}}</ref> On January 4, 2018, The CW and [[Warner Bros Television]] released the first look at Nafessa Williams as Anissa Pierce in her official [[Thunder (DC Comics)|Thunder]] superhero costume.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2018/01/black-lightning-thunder-first-look-photo-nafessa-williams-cw-1202236106/|title='Black Lightning': First-Look Photo Of Nafessa Williams As Thunder In CW Series|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=Pedersen|first=Erik|date=January 4, 2018|access-date=April 14, 2019|archive-date=April 13, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190413095055/https://deadline.com/2018/01/black-lightning-thunder-first-look-photo-nafessa-williams-cw-1202236106/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine|url=https://ew.com/tv/2018/01/04/black-lightning-first-look-thunder/|title=Black Lightning unveils first look at Thunder|magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]|last=Agard|first=Chancellor|date=January 4, 2018|access-date=April 14, 2019|archive-date=April 14, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190414171726/https://ew.com/tv/2018/01/04/black-lightning-first-look-thunder/|url-status=live}}</ref> On March 25, the producers and writers of the season attended the 2018 [[WonderCon]] and screened the episode "Sins of the Father: The Book of Redemption" at their panel ahead of its official debut on The CW.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2018/02/the-100-black-lightning-krypton-dc-comics-wondercon-warner-bros-tv-1202305784/|title='Black Lightning', 'Krypton', 'The 100' & More Part Of WBTV's WonderCon Footprint|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|last=D'Alessandro|first=Anthony|date=February 28, 2018|access-date=April 14, 2019|archive-date=April 14, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190414171727/https://deadline.com/2018/02/the-100-black-lightning-krypton-dc-comics-wondercon-warner-bros-tv-1202305784/|url-status=live}}</ref> The main cast of the second season as well as the Akils attended San Diego Comic-Con on July 21 to promote the season.<ref name="Calloway" /><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2018/06/warner-bros-tv-comic-con-riverdale-arrow-black-lightning-big-bang-theory-castle-rock-the-flash-supernatural-1202416527/|title=Comic-Con: Warner Bros TV Goes Big With 'Riverdale' Hall H Debut, 'Arrow' Return, 'Black Lightning' + More|last=Ramos|first=Dino-Ray|date=June 25, 2018|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180625221834/https://deadline.com/2018/06/warner-bros-tv-comic-con-riverdale-arrow-black-lightning-big-bang-theory-castle-rock-the-flash-supernatural-1202416527/|archive-date=June 25, 2018|url-status=live|access-date=July 11, 2018}}</ref> The first trailer of the season was released on September 6.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://comicbook.com/dc/2018/09/05/black-lightning-season-2-trailer/|title='Black Lightning' Season 2 Trailer Released|website=ComicBook.com|last=Aguilar|first=Matthew|date=September 6, 2018|access-date=September 24, 2019|archive-date=September 24, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190924213853/https://comicbook.com/dc/2018/09/05/black-lightning-season-2-trailer/|url-status=live}}</ref> On December 13, The CW released the first promotional image of China Anne McClain as Jennifer Pierce in her official [[Lightning (DC Comics)|Lightning]] superhero costume.<ref name="Lightning" /><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://tvline.com/2018/12/13/black-lightning-jennifer-costume-lightning/|title=Black Lightning's Jennifer Super Suits Up — Your First Look at Lightning|website=[[TVLine]]|last=Mitovich|first=Matt Webb|date=December 13, 2018|access-date=March 18, 2019|archive-date=March 1, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190301030900/https://tvline.com/2018/12/13/black-lightning-jennifer-costume-lightning/|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine|url=https://ew.com/tv/2018/12/13/black-lightning-jennifer-lightning-first-look/|title=Black Lightning reveals first look at Jennifer suiting up as Lightning|magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]|last=Agard|first=Chancellor|date=December 13, 2018|access-date=March 18, 2019|archive-date=April 15, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190415023101/https://ew.com/tv/2018/12/13/black-lightning-jennifer-lightning-first-look/|url-status=live}}</ref> Several of the main cast members of the third season attended San Diego Comic-Con on July 20, 2019, to promote the season.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.cbr.com/black-lightning-sdcc-2019-panel/|title=Black Lightning Strikes At SDCC With Season 3 Details|website=[[Comic Book Resources|CBR]]|last=Damore|first=Meagan|date=July 20, 2019|access-date=July 20, 2019|archive-date=July 21, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190721022732/https://www.cbr.com/black-lightning-sdcc-2019-panel/|url-status=live}}</ref> The first trailer of the season was released on September 24.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://comicbook.com/dc/2019/09/24/black-lightning-season-3-trailer/|title=Black Lightning Season 3 Extended Trailer Teases New Suit|website=ComicBook.com|last=Lovett|first=Jamie|date=September 24, 2019|access-date=September 24, 2019|archive-date=September 24, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190924213858/https://comicbook.com/dc/2019/09/24/black-lightning-season-3-trailer/|url-status=live}}</ref>

